Date: Thu, 5 Dec 2024 09:51:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HACK: winedmo/media-converter: Implement media converter
 demuxer.

(cherry picked from commit ddc984784061b51d5e262de08890c2f867efa7bd)
mproton-resolved: 11.20 reordered demuxer_destroy() to free the stream filters before the format context; that order is kept, with params->context taken from the new demuxer->stream_context, since the media-converter path replaces the AVIOContext. 11.20's new MP4 stream-name parsing reads the stream context the same way. Fixes in Proton's code: mediaconv_demuxer_open() now clears *ctx after freeing it (otherwise, with no transcoded entry and no MEDIACONV_BLANK_VIDEO_FILE, the default outside Proton, demuxer_create()'s failure path freed the context a second time), frees its hash buffer, and the operator precedence in demuxer_create()'s 'if ((ret = mediaconv_demuxer_open(...) < 0))' is fixed so the error code is logged.
